  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human Development Monitoring and Evaluation Services Provider</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of the human development monitoring and evaluation services (HDMES) provider will be to provide high-quality advice and independent monitoring and evaluation services at investment and whole-of-program level to the Health, and Education and Leadership programs in PNG.  

The Monitoring and Evaluation (M&amp;E) functions required under the HDMES 
are:
a) Advise and verifying baselines and M&amp;E frameworks of investments
b) Conduct annual reporting on Portfolio Program progress
c) Produce high quality, tailored communications products based on analysis
d) Quality assure analysis and reports produced by DFAT, and by partners as directed by DFAT
e) Conduct independent evaluations of DFAT investments, as directed by DFAT
f) Ad hoc M&amp;E support to PNG Government partners, as directed by DFAT. Sector split: 120-Health 70%, 110-Education 30%.</narrative>
  </description>
